    description: "The INV-numat closure diagnostic (per-cohort validation_report + literal/broader kind-grep) PROVABLY UNDERCOUNTS: it missed proto rpc/service (positional helper) and historically message/grpc_* (assignment form). So violation counts are a FLOOR, not a ceiling, and a zero-on-a-cohort result does NOT prove the invariant holds. Before INV-numat can close: sweep ALL analyzer emit sites for the pattern 'a raw tree-sitter node.type / literal flows into an evidence_type or kind PARAMETER (kwarg, assignment, OR positional helper)', across languages the cohorts have not exercised (php/csharp/scala/kotlin/swift/dart/elixir). This is the structural prerequisite to a trustworthy zero, replacing per-cohort violation-counting."  # 4cf8
